### ----- 2.5 OPTIMISTIC LOCKING ON AN EMPLOYEE -----
### A PUT carries every field, so an update built on a stale copy carries
### the values as they were when the form was opened.

### 2.5.1 Read Maya — expect 200, version 0 and 40 hours
# @name 2.5.1 Read Maya — expect 200, version 0 and 40 hours
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 2.5.2 Manager A cuts her hours to 32, sending version 0
###       expect 200, version becomes 1
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0, "fullName": "מאיה כהן", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 32, "jobPositionId": 2}

### 2.5.3 Manager B still holds version 0 and only meant to fix the name
###       expect 409 — the check stops the 40 hours coming back
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0, "fullName": "מאיה כהן-לוי", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 2}

### 2.5.4 Reload — expect 200, version 1 and 32 hours
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 2.5.5 Retry with version 1, keeping the 32 hours — expect 200
###       The version stays at 1, because Hibernate raises it when a field
###       is written to and this sends the values back unchanged
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 1, "fullName": "מאיה כהן", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 32, "jobPositionId": 2}

### 2.5.6 Put her back to 40 for the rest of the run — expect 200
###       version 1 again, and this one does change a field
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 1, "fullName": "מאיה כהן", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 2}


### ----- 2.6 THE LAST MANAGER CANNOT BE REMOVED -----
### Dana is the only manager. Standing her down and demoting her are both
### refused, and the count is read under a write lock so two demotions
### arriving together cannot both pass.
###
### A demotion takes effect at once, so whoever demotes themselves has to
### hand over to the other manager before carrying on.

### 2.6.1 Stand her down — expect 400
# @name 2.6.1 Stand her down — expect 400
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1?version=0
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 2.6.2 Read Dana — expect 200, note the version
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 2.6.3 Demote her to EMPLOYEE — expect 400
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0, "fullName": "דנה לוי", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.4 Promote Yoni — expect 200, now there are two managers
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/2
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0, "fullName": "יוני ברק", "role": "MANAGER",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.5 Now Dana can be demoted — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0, "fullName": "דנה לוי", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.6 Dana is an employee from here on, so the rest needs Yoni's session
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "yoni@shiftscheduler.local", "password": "password123"}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        const cookie = response.headers.valueOf("Set-Cookie");
        client.global.set("token", cookie.split(";")[0].split("=")[1]);
    }
%}

### 2.6.7 And Yoni, now the only one, cannot — expect 400
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/2
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 1, "fullName": "יוני ברק", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.8 Restore Dana as manager — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 1, "fullName": "דנה לוי", "role": "MANAGER",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.9 Demote Yoni back — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/2
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 1, "fullName": "יוני ברק", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.10 And Yoni is an employee now, so back to Dana
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana@shiftscheduler.local", "password": "password123"}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        const cookie = response.headers.valueOf("Set-Cookie");
        client.global.set("token", cookie.split(";")[0].split("=")[1]);
    }
%}

### 2.6.11 Stand the new employee down — expect 204
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/employees/11?version=1
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 2.6.12 And bring them back — expect 200, active true again
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/11/activate?version=2
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### ----- 2.7 LEAVES -----

### 2.7.1 Omer on leave 24-26 Aug — expect 201, one range of 3 days
# @name 2.7.1 Omer on leave 24-26 Aug — expect 201, one range of 3 days
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"employeeId": 4, "startDate": "2026-08-24", "endDate": "2026-08-26", "type": "VACATION"}

### 2.7.2 Overlapping range — expect 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"employeeId": 4, "startDate": "2026-08-26", "endDate": "2026-08-28", "type": "SICK"}

### 2.7.3 A range longer than a year — expect 400
###       Guards against a mistyped year, since a row is saved per day
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"employeeId": 4, "startDate": "2026-09-01", "endDate": "2027-10-01", "type": "VACATION"}

### 2.7.4 End before start — expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"employeeId": 4, "startDate": "2026-09-04", "endDate": "2026-09-02", "type": "SICK"}

### 2.7.5 List — expect 200, Omer's new range beside the three the
###       seed put in the weeks before this one
GET http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 2.7.6 A range for Shira — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"employeeId": 5, "startDate": "2026-09-07", "endDate": "2026-09-08", "type": "SICK"}

### 2.7.7 List again — read the id of Shira's first day
GET http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 2.7.8 Remove that one day by id — expect 204
###       A range is stored a row per day, so the other one stays
###       Replace the id with the one 2.7.7 returned
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/leaves/8
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 2.7.9 Remove what is left of the range — expect 204
###       This one takes dates rather than an id, the way the screen does it
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/leaves?employeeId=5&from=2026-09-07&to=2026-09-08
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 2.7.10 List again — expect 200, Shira is back to the day the seed gave her
GET http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Cookie: access_token={{token}}


### ===========================================================
### 3 — CREATING A WEEK (status COLLECTING)
### ===========================================================

### 3.1 Create the week of 23 Aug — expect 201, 21 shifts,
###     status COLLECTING, version 0
# @name 3.1 Create the week of 23 Aug — expect 201, 21 shifts,
POST http://localhost:8080/api/schedules
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{
  "weekStart": "2026-08-23",
  "shifts": [
    { "shiftTypeId": 1, "requirements": [
      {"jobPositionId": 1, "requiredCount": 1},
      {"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 2}
    ]},
    { "shiftTypeId": 2, "requirements": [
      {"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 2}
    ]},
    { "shiftTypeId": 3, "requirements": [
      {"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 1}
    ]}
  ]
}

### 3.2 List — expect 200, status COLLECTING
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 3.3 Detail — expect 200, shifts from 2026-08-23 to 2026-08-29
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 3.8 Assigning while COLLECTING — expect 409, wrong status
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"shiftId": 64, "employeeId": 3, "override": false, "scheduleVersion": 0}


### ----- 3.9 OPTIMISTIC LOCKING ON REQUIREMENTS -----

### 3.9.1 Edit requirements with the current version 0 — expect 200
###       This raises the version to 1
# @name 3.9.1 Edit requirements with the current version 0 — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/shifts/64/requirements
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0, "requirements": [
  {"jobPositionId": 1, "requiredCount": 1},
  {"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 3},
  {"jobPositionId": 3, "requiredCount": 1}
]}

### 3.9.2 Send version 0 again — expect 409, someone else changed it
###       This is the stale-client case
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/shifts/64/requirements
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0, "requirements": [{"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 2}]}

### 3.9.3 Read the current version — expect 200, version 1
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 3.9.4 Retry with version 1 — expect 200, version becomes 2
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/shifts/64/requirements
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 1, "requirements": [
  {"jobPositionId": 1, "requiredCount": 1},
  {"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 3},
  {"jobPositionId": 3, "requiredCount": 1}
]}

### 3.9.5 Clear the requirements of the last shift — expect 204
###       This raises the version to 4
POST http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/requirements/clear
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 2, "shiftIds": [84]}

### 3.9.6 Same job position twice — expect 400
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/shifts/64/requirements
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 3, "requirements": [
  {"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 1},
  {"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 2}
]}

### 3.9.7 Unknown shift — expect 404
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/shifts/999/requirements
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 3, "requirements": [{"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 1}]}


