Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 4.10.4 Lock the schedule — expect 403
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/lock
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 3}

### 4.10.5 Coverage — expect 403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/coverage
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### 4.10.6 Assign someone — expect 403
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"shiftId": 69, "employeeId": 3, "override": false, "scheduleVersion": 3}


### ===========================================================
### 5 — CLOSING SUBMISSION (COLLECTING -> DRAFT)
### ===========================================================

### 5.0 Back to the manager
# @name 5.0 Back to the manager
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana@shiftscheduler.local", "password": "password123"}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        const cookie = response.headers.valueOf("Set-Cookie");
        client.global.set("token", cookie.split(";")[0].split("=")[1]);
    }
%}

### 5.1 Lock with a stale version — expect 409
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/lock
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0}

### 5.2 Lock with the current version 3 — expect 200, status DRAFT
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/lock
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 3}

### 5.3 Lock again — expect 409, it is no longer COLLECTING
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/lock
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 4}

### 5.4 The manager can still correct a constraint — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences
